From fc81259d4422511a6d2b7f4f6a3012b2e667b2dd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: WeiguangTWK <weiguangtwk@outlook.com>
Date: Sat, 4 Jul 2026 09:48:15 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Neko LineageOS: Allow Updater app to recognize Full update
 and incremental update
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Usually there is only Full update in LineageOS OFFICIAL, but when it comes to update engine of AOSP it allow user to
install incremental update to reduce file size to download. For incremental update there should be a 'base version' of it to
judge whether this update is suitable for currently running version which is missing in LineageOS updater. I add the
ability to judge by introduce a new key 'minBaseTimestamp'

Now adapted to New composed Updater app

Only dislay when incremental updates satisfy minBaseTimestamp ≤ CurrentBuildTime(ro.build.date.utc) ≤ UpdateTimestamp(datetime)

Change-Id: I85a82020de72971ec6e2875c9dd9b19cdc3bd97e
